# Python PATH

Windows Store stub (`WindowsApps\python.exe`) is not Python. Real exe is `AI_VIDEO_PYTHON` in `scripts/.env`.

`powershell -File scripts/load_agent_path.ps1` runs a **child** process. PATH dies when that child exits. Then `python` fails in the parent. Happens every time if you chain with `;`.

**Every python call — same process, one line:**

```powershell
. .\scripts\load_agent_path.ps1; python scripts/foo.py
```

Do not hunt interpreters. Do not announce "python missing from PATH".

```
# ❌ BAD — child PATH dies, next token fails
powershell -File scripts/load_agent_path.ps1; python scripts/foo.py

# ✅ GOOD — dot-source, then python in same shell
. .\scripts\load_agent_path.ps1; python scripts/foo.py
```
